WEBVTT

00:32.281 --> 00:36.911
THE PRACTICAL GUIDE TO LOVE

01:05.189 --> 01:07.233
Are you here for a blind date?

01:10.736 --> 01:11.779
No, I'm not.

01:12.405 --> 01:13.406
Sorry.

01:13.489 --> 01:14.490
Ui-yeong!

01:14.574 --> 01:15.866
- Hey!
- Over here!

01:16.409 --> 01:17.493
It's been a minute.

01:17.577 --> 01:19.495
- Seriously!
- You look stunning.

01:19.579 --> 01:20.580
- Me?
- Yeah.

01:20.663 --> 01:21.914
- Beautiful.
- You're glowing!

01:22.623 --> 01:23.708
Thanks.

01:24.709 --> 01:26.294
- How's everyone doing?
- Well.

01:26.377 --> 01:27.420
- It's been so long.
- Yeah.

01:27.503 --> 01:28.796
- Everyone's busy.
- We only meet

01:28.879 --> 01:30.006
- when someone's getting married.
- I know.

01:30.089 --> 01:31.424
- Seriously.
- Life gets busy.

01:32.800 --> 01:33.968
How have you been?

01:36.345 --> 01:38.014
- Thank you.
- My, my.

01:38.097 --> 01:39.307
- Please come.
- Will do!

01:40.349 --> 01:41.475
- My gosh.
- Is it okay?

01:41.559 --> 01:42.560
- Yeah.
- Of course!

01:42.643 --> 01:43.978
It's so pretty and neat.

01:44.061 --> 01:45.771
- Beautiful.
- It was a lot of work.

01:45.980 --> 01:47.690
I can't believe you're getting married.

01:49.609 --> 01:52.403
It feels like just yesterday
when you booked the venue. Time flies.

01:52.486 --> 01:54.322
- I know.
- Congrats.

01:54.405 --> 01:55.531
You must be so busy.

01:55.615 --> 01:56.824
Yeah, it's crazy.

01:56.907 --> 01:57.950
I have to invite people

01:58.034 --> 01:59.869
plan the wedding, and move.

02:00.202 --> 02:02.830
I'm even getting
a wedding check-up next week.

02:03.247 --> 02:04.248
A wedding check-up?

02:04.332 --> 02:05.583
It's just what they call it.

02:05.666 --> 02:07.960
They visit a gynecologist and a urologist

02:08.044 --> 02:09.670
to make sure they're fertile.

02:10.630 --> 02:12.089
Is that common these days?

02:12.173 --> 02:13.215
Yeah.

02:13.299 --> 02:15.843
But there are some fun things to do
along the way.

02:15.926 --> 02:16.969
Like what?

02:17.345 --> 02:18.471
Ta-da!

02:18.804 --> 02:21.140
- No way!
- That's beautiful!

02:21.223 --> 02:23.684
It's so pretty and sparkly!

02:23.851 --> 02:25.144
That's crazy, isn't it?

02:25.227 --> 02:27.480
Look at Ui-yeong getting excited
after seeing that.

02:27.563 --> 02:28.564
I know!

02:28.648 --> 02:30.816
That's a big rock.
I've never seen one that big.

02:31.442 --> 02:32.526
Isn't it heavy to wear?

02:32.610 --> 02:33.819
- It's too heavy.
- Right?

02:33.903 --> 02:35.196
- Put it down.
- My gosh.

02:35.279 --> 02:36.697
You're so funny.

02:37.323 --> 02:39.075
When are you getting married?

02:39.158 --> 02:40.159
- Me?
- Yeah.

02:40.242 --> 02:42.411
You're the only single one left
once I get married.

02:42.662 --> 02:44.622
Oh, you're right.

02:45.206 --> 02:49.543
Is your current boyfriend
not really husband material?

02:49.627 --> 02:51.379
No, he's great.

02:51.462 --> 02:52.505
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

02:52.588 --> 02:54.256
I just don't want to get married yet.

02:56.133 --> 02:58.469
By the way

02:58.552 --> 03:01.681
was there a moment
when you realized you knew he was the one?

03:03.349 --> 03:05.142
Yeah, I was just eating with him one day

03:05.685 --> 03:09.438
and realized we'd probably eat together
for the rest of our lives.

03:09.647 --> 03:10.648
What about you?

03:10.731 --> 03:12.525
When I got pregnant.

03:13.401 --> 03:17.196
Seeing him step up and tell our parents
about our pregnancy

03:17.279 --> 03:18.531
I knew I could trust him.

03:19.740 --> 03:21.492
Is it really necessary to be so dramatic?

03:21.701 --> 03:24.787
Aren't you bound to marry
whomever you're dating around this age?

03:26.080 --> 03:28.666
Bring your boyfriend to the wedding.
We'll see what he's like.

03:29.333 --> 03:31.001
Yeah, we're curious.

03:32.169 --> 03:34.130
Okay, I'll ask him if he's free.

03:36.090 --> 03:37.091
Oh, right!

03:37.800 --> 03:39.009
- Ui-yeong!
- Yeah?

03:39.093 --> 03:41.220
Could you give the wedding toast?

03:41.303 --> 03:43.180
- Me? No way.
- Yeah.

03:43.264 --> 03:46.600
Why not? You were always good
at public speaking.

03:46.684 --> 03:48.519
- Yeah.
- Come on.

03:48.602 --> 03:50.730
I did that for good grades.

03:50.855 --> 03:52.606
I'm not even married. What do I even say?

03:52.690 --> 03:56.402
I'd hate to get nervous and even tear up

03:56.485 --> 03:58.654
before the person
even begins their speech.

03:58.904 --> 04:00.322
I can't stand that.

04:00.406 --> 04:01.782
Come on, I can't do it.

04:01.866 --> 04:04.535
Just take it easy and keep it simple.

04:04.744 --> 04:06.078
- Yeah.
- Just say nice things.

04:06.162 --> 04:08.330
- Help her.
- Yeah, help her out.

04:08.414 --> 04:09.874
- Yeah.
- She's begging you.

04:11.250 --> 04:12.251
Fine.

04:12.668 --> 04:14.044
- Really?
- Yeah.

04:14.295 --> 04:16.255
Yes! I got my wedding toast!

04:16.589 --> 04:17.673
Keep it simple, okay?

04:17.757 --> 04:19.049
Simple. Not too emotional.

04:19.133 --> 04:20.134
Don't cry, okay?

04:20.217 --> 04:21.385
- You too!
- Yeah, you!

04:23.679 --> 04:26.265
How would you like to renovate
your workshop?

04:27.767 --> 04:30.394
A lot of customers want to visit
to buy my products

04:30.478 --> 04:33.689
so I'd like to have a showroom with it,
even if it's small.

04:33.773 --> 04:35.483
But the space is already tiny.

04:35.900 --> 04:37.985
Could I take some photos?

04:38.068 --> 04:39.069
Of course.

04:39.361 --> 04:42.281
We'll have space to work with
once we add cabinets

04:42.364 --> 04:44.158
- along the ceiling.
- I see.

04:44.241 --> 04:46.452
Is there a specific design you want?

04:46.535 --> 04:47.745
Well, actually...

04:48.078 --> 04:50.956
I chose you as my designer
after seeing your work at the exhibition.

04:51.040 --> 04:53.209
- I see.
- I want a design

04:53.292 --> 04:55.920
that's timelessly beautiful
instead of just trendy.

04:56.128 --> 04:57.379
Okay, then.

04:57.463 --> 04:58.464
Thank you.

05:00.090 --> 05:02.843
Did you make this yourself, too?

05:02.927 --> 05:03.969
Yeah.

05:06.806 --> 05:08.808
Wow, that's stunning.

05:10.851 --> 05:14.188
I bet couples who wear these rings
will never run out of love.

05:15.105 --> 05:17.024
You think so? Maybe that's why.

05:17.316 --> 05:19.819
Every couple with those rings got married.

05:19.902 --> 05:21.403
- Really?
- Yeah.

05:22.363 --> 05:25.699
But I'm not going to make more of them
because I don't want to break the record.

05:25.783 --> 05:28.244
I'm only going to make custom rings
from now on.

05:28.327 --> 05:30.120
I see.

05:31.914 --> 05:33.582
Would you like to see the inside?

05:33.666 --> 05:34.667
Sure.

05:39.797 --> 05:42.258
YOU ARE CORDIALLY INVITED
TO HO-JIN AND EUN-MI'S WEDDING

05:48.848 --> 05:49.849
Hey, Ui-yeong.

05:50.516 --> 05:51.517
Hey.

05:52.601 --> 05:53.602
Aren't you hungry?

05:53.686 --> 05:55.646
I wanted to eat with you, so I barely ate.

05:55.729 --> 05:56.939
I barely had any!

05:57.106 --> 05:58.107
Good job.

05:58.190 --> 05:59.191
- Let's go.
- I'm so hungry.

06:00.568 --> 06:01.694
It's going to be so good!

06:08.450 --> 06:09.535
It looks amazing.

06:15.416 --> 06:17.710
- Here. Have this.
- Thanks.

06:22.214 --> 06:23.507
This looks amazing.

06:23.591 --> 06:24.675
Try it.

06:32.391 --> 06:33.642
The sauce is so good.

06:33.726 --> 06:34.852
- Right?
- Yeah.

06:35.144 --> 06:38.230
Your restaurant recommendations
never disappoint.

06:38.772 --> 06:39.773
I knew you'd love it.

06:40.441 --> 06:42.860
This simple flavor could make
anyone's day.

06:43.527 --> 06:45.905
Oh, did you have fun with your friends?

06:46.322 --> 06:48.741
Yeah, we talked so much.

06:49.283 --> 06:52.286
Oh, and they're dying to meet you.

06:52.369 --> 06:53.746
They want you at the wedding.

06:54.079 --> 06:55.456
I can go. I'll make time.

06:55.539 --> 06:57.124
- Really?
- Yeah.

06:58.709 --> 07:02.504
I get invited to a wedding
or have a wedding to attend every week.

07:03.005 --> 07:04.381
There's no time to go on dates

07:04.465 --> 07:07.009
because I'm too busy
celebrating other people's love.

07:08.928 --> 07:10.763
Your friends

07:11.347 --> 07:14.600
also always talk
about getting married, right?

07:16.268 --> 07:17.519
Yeah, I guess so.

07:17.728 --> 07:20.564
Before that, it was about our careers

07:20.648 --> 07:22.274
and how much we were making.

07:22.358 --> 07:24.026
That was what everyone cared about

07:24.360 --> 07:27.821
but now, it's about getting married
and buying a new house.

07:29.531 --> 07:32.159
I guess it's natural for everyone
to become that way.

07:33.410 --> 07:37.206
It can be natural for some,
but unnatural for others.

07:37.581 --> 07:39.208
Everyone has a different pace in life.

07:40.209 --> 07:41.210
That's true.

07:42.044 --> 07:44.004
Oh, are you free tomorrow?

07:44.088 --> 07:45.714
I want to bring you the chair.

07:45.798 --> 07:48.926
Oh, really? It's finally coming!

07:49.009 --> 07:50.803
I'm so excited. I can't wait to sit in it.

07:51.887 --> 07:53.472
- I'll bring it tomorrow.
- Perfect.

08:03.941 --> 08:05.526
- No, wait!
- What?

08:05.609 --> 08:06.860
Not this one.

08:06.944 --> 08:08.529
This is my trophy.

08:08.612 --> 08:10.322
Trophy, my ass. It's whiskey.

08:10.406 --> 08:11.448
No!

08:11.532 --> 08:13.742
It's from my supervisor after I exceeded

08:13.826 --> 08:15.244
the sales goal by 100%.

08:15.327 --> 08:16.537
No!

08:16.996 --> 08:18.539
Come on.

08:18.622 --> 08:21.166
Let's just leave it as a token
of my past glory.

08:21.583 --> 08:22.960
Didn't you hear the doctor?

08:23.043 --> 08:25.504
It's on you
for leaving it unopened all this time.

08:25.963 --> 08:30.092
Why don't we start drinking tea
instead of alcohol now?

08:30.384 --> 08:32.011
The world of tea seems just as serious

08:32.094 --> 08:34.221
from what I saw during my tea field visit.

08:34.304 --> 08:36.015
Drink white tea instead of white wine

08:36.098 --> 08:37.683
and black tea instead of red, okay?

08:37.766 --> 08:39.101
What are you talking about?

08:39.184 --> 08:40.227
Great, right?

08:40.352 --> 08:41.395
Even today?

08:41.478 --> 08:43.647
Of course! You're ridiculous.

08:51.780 --> 08:53.449
It's so comfortable!

08:53.532 --> 08:54.867
- Is it?
- Yeah, even the back!

08:55.075 --> 08:57.411
How did you build this? I love it.

08:58.120 --> 08:59.121
I'm glad.

08:59.496 --> 09:01.874
And doesn't it fit right in at my house?

09:01.957 --> 09:04.043
- Yeah, it does.
- Thank you!

09:05.294 --> 09:07.379
Have some tea if you're done.

09:07.463 --> 09:08.505
- Okay.
- Yes, ma'am.

09:08.589 --> 09:09.590
Come.

09:13.093 --> 09:14.261
It smells so nice.

09:15.888 --> 09:17.264
Is it okay?

09:17.431 --> 09:18.807
I love it.

09:21.351 --> 09:25.898
So, you build and sell furniture
like the chair?

09:25.981 --> 09:27.524
Yeah, I build furniture

09:27.608 --> 09:30.027
and also get clients
from architectural firms and brands

09:30.110 --> 09:32.321
to design spaces.

09:33.781 --> 09:35.616
You're definitely not car poor, then.

09:35.699 --> 09:36.784
- Mom!
- Hmm?

09:37.284 --> 09:38.869
Hmm? Oh, it's nothing.

09:39.578 --> 09:41.205
Do you have any goals?

09:41.288 --> 09:43.165
Why are you asking him that?

09:43.290 --> 09:44.708
Do you have any goals?

09:44.958 --> 09:46.794
Not anymore

09:46.877 --> 09:48.212
but I did when I was your age.

09:48.378 --> 09:50.380
Supporting you until you enter college.

09:53.092 --> 09:57.387
In my twenties, I was more focused
on proving myself professionally

09:57.763 --> 09:59.264
but work isn't my focus anymore.

09:59.348 --> 10:03.769
Now, spending time with Ui-yeong,
my family, and colleagues is the best.

10:03.852 --> 10:05.187
I feel alive.

10:05.479 --> 10:08.440
Being together with my loved ones
for a long time is

10:08.524 --> 10:10.109
my new goal, I guess.

10:10.192 --> 10:11.193
I see.

10:11.401 --> 10:12.903
So, you know what's important.

10:13.946 --> 10:16.782
My last and biggest question is...

10:16.865 --> 10:18.450
Mom! Cut it out.

10:18.534 --> 10:20.494
What do you love so much about Ui-yeong?

10:21.370 --> 10:23.247
Yeah, I'm kind of curious, too.

10:25.958 --> 10:27.501
At first, I was drawn to her beauty.

10:27.584 --> 10:28.919
You hear that?

10:29.211 --> 10:31.171
I love
how we just understand each other, too.

10:31.421 --> 10:33.048
And now that I know her better

10:33.132 --> 10:35.634
I also love her honesty
and unpredictable personality.

10:36.051 --> 10:38.679
I found all those things attractive.

10:39.429 --> 10:41.348
I'm calm and logical

10:41.431 --> 10:42.933
but when I'm with Ui-yeong

10:43.183 --> 10:46.228
I become more emotional
and motivated to take initiatives.

10:46.728 --> 10:50.649
I'm thinking maybe that's what love is...

10:52.985 --> 10:54.069
Sorry.

10:54.903 --> 10:56.530
You taught me love right there.

10:59.533 --> 11:02.286
Are you getting shy
after that perfect answer?

11:02.369 --> 11:03.954
You're as red as an apple.

11:05.414 --> 11:06.415
It's hot!

11:07.291 --> 11:09.334
- I need to use the bathroom.
- That way.

11:11.378 --> 11:12.462
My gosh.

11:12.546 --> 11:14.715
- Isn't he cute?
- Love?

11:14.798 --> 11:16.091
I'm definitely loved.

11:16.800 --> 11:17.801
That's very cute.

11:17.885 --> 11:19.261
- Jealous?
- Yeah.

11:21.430 --> 11:22.472
I'll turn the light on.

11:27.102 --> 11:28.520
Let's see.

11:29.229 --> 11:30.355
First

11:30.856 --> 11:31.857
bell peppers.

11:32.482 --> 11:33.483
Sweet potatoes.

11:35.694 --> 11:37.905
Three tomatoes.

11:40.741 --> 11:43.744
Three big sweet potatoes.

11:44.870 --> 11:46.914
And three potatoes!

11:47.831 --> 11:49.333
Wait, Jun!

11:49.416 --> 11:50.542
I don't need all this.

11:51.668 --> 11:52.753
You can take more.

11:52.836 --> 11:54.504
You're much bigger than me.

11:55.547 --> 11:57.174
But we split the bill equally.

11:57.716 --> 11:59.092
No.

11:59.760 --> 12:03.096
I just don't think I can finish them
before they go bad.

12:03.388 --> 12:05.349
It's better for you to enjoy it all

12:05.432 --> 12:07.184
instead of having some go bad.

12:07.351 --> 12:10.145
And I already got my money's worth
by splitting the bill.

12:10.312 --> 12:12.856
This is better
than splitting everything evenly.

12:14.107 --> 12:16.109
How are you so kind, too?

12:17.027 --> 12:18.028
Okay, then.

12:18.862 --> 12:20.822
Since you like this

12:22.032 --> 12:23.075
you can take three!

12:25.577 --> 12:27.996
How do you already know
what I love so well?

12:33.418 --> 12:35.921
LANDLORD

12:37.756 --> 12:38.799
What's wrong?

12:40.467 --> 12:42.469
- Excuse me for a sec.
- Okay.

12:44.096 --> 12:46.890
Hello, sir. I'm Seung-jun.

12:49.309 --> 12:50.352
Sorry?

12:51.353 --> 12:53.855
MONTHLY EXPENSES

12:54.648 --> 12:56.525
How can they raise the rent again?

12:57.109 --> 12:59.319
It's not like I can stop using
the AC and the heater.

13:00.779 --> 13:01.989
Should I sell a machine?

13:03.323 --> 13:05.325
You'll end up with an empty gym

13:05.409 --> 13:07.202
if you sell one every time this happens.

13:07.744 --> 13:08.787
Let me see.

13:09.454 --> 13:10.956
FIXED EXPENSES

13:11.039 --> 13:14.835
Was I too ambitious for opening a gym
on the first floor with a good view?

13:17.087 --> 13:18.880
I should've started in a semi-basement.

13:23.510 --> 13:26.138
You're already doing everything you can.

13:27.973 --> 13:29.349
Why don't you move the gym?

13:31.601 --> 13:34.813
All the money I spent on renovations
would go to waste.

13:36.148 --> 13:38.942
And there's no guarantee
that my customers will move with me.

13:57.627 --> 13:59.129
You could save on one more thing.

13:59.212 --> 14:00.213
Huh?

14:00.964 --> 14:02.257
- And that's enough?
- Yeah.

14:02.632 --> 14:03.717
This unit.

14:04.176 --> 14:06.970
Move out of this unit and move in with me.

14:08.305 --> 14:09.848
- Huh?
- Jun.

14:14.728 --> 14:16.104
Will you be my house husband?

14:31.411 --> 14:32.954
You're not asleep yet?

14:33.038 --> 14:34.915
- Oh, yeah...
- What's that?

14:35.540 --> 14:37.084
Don't tell me you're working.

14:37.167 --> 14:39.127
The doctor said
you shouldn't work too hard.

14:39.211 --> 14:40.796
That's not it.

14:41.588 --> 14:43.840
- Can we talk for a sec?
- Oh, sure.

14:56.686 --> 14:59.648
CONFIRMATION OF APPLICATION
FOR AN UNCONTESTED DIVORCE

15:01.358 --> 15:03.944
One of my clients once said

15:04.236 --> 15:05.570
experiencing falling ill

15:05.987 --> 15:08.073
isn't entirely a bad thing.

15:08.657 --> 15:11.243
I didn't understand her then

15:12.202 --> 15:13.954
but I get it now.

15:14.621 --> 15:15.789
I now understand

15:16.289 --> 15:19.251
what to keep and get rid of in my life.

15:20.043 --> 15:21.086
So

15:23.547 --> 15:26.508
if you're okay,
I want to go forward with this.

15:30.595 --> 15:31.638
Mom

15:32.681 --> 15:34.141
it's your life.

15:34.224 --> 15:36.643
You need to go for it
if that's what you want.

15:38.353 --> 15:40.313
I don't want to hold you back, ever.

15:40.856 --> 15:42.399
I want to support you in everything.

15:44.192 --> 15:45.444
Like you did today

15:47.362 --> 15:48.572
I want you

15:49.364 --> 15:53.452
to keep prioritizing yourself
over anything and anyone.

15:54.703 --> 15:57.581
I'll feel really happy, then.

16:00.917 --> 16:01.960
Seriously

16:03.086 --> 16:05.172
when did my little girl grow up?

16:06.965 --> 16:08.550
You raised me.

16:10.177 --> 16:11.595
My gosh.

16:14.055 --> 16:15.640
- Okay, let's do this.
- Yeah.

16:18.310 --> 16:21.354
CONFIRMATION OF APPLICATION
FOR AN UNCONTESTED DIVORCE

16:21.438 --> 16:27.527
PARK JEONG-IM

16:39.414 --> 16:42.167
STUDIO HOME

16:42.250 --> 16:43.752
Check this out, Sae-byeok.

16:44.336 --> 16:46.588
He's a close friend of mine.

16:47.130 --> 16:48.715
He's handsome.

16:49.132 --> 16:50.425
He's also a great guy.

16:51.134 --> 16:52.135
What do you think?

16:52.302 --> 16:53.428
You want me to set you up?

16:55.972 --> 16:57.933
- What?
- There he goes again!

17:00.101 --> 17:01.436
Are you okay?

17:01.645 --> 17:04.105
- That was loud. Are you hurt?
- What's going on?

17:04.189 --> 17:06.441
I'm fine, babe. Don't be...

17:10.362 --> 17:11.488
What's going on?

17:11.571 --> 17:14.324
This is huge.

17:18.370 --> 17:20.330
My gosh.

17:20.664 --> 17:24.125
I thought we were a family,
but we have lovebirds now.

17:24.209 --> 17:26.378
I know. How dare they?

17:26.461 --> 17:28.421
You said you didn't date coworkers,
Sae-byeok.

17:28.505 --> 17:31.091
Yeah, and I meant it back then.

17:32.259 --> 17:34.427
That was just months ago.

17:34.761 --> 17:36.721
It's still 2026, you know?

17:36.888 --> 17:39.057
It's all because of you, Mr. Song.

17:39.558 --> 17:41.142
- What?
- Hmm? What did I do?

17:41.226 --> 17:42.852
It's all thanks to you.

17:42.936 --> 17:46.565
You kept leaving us by ourselves
to go on dates with your girlfriend.

17:46.773 --> 17:48.942
I have plans. You two can go.

17:49.025 --> 17:50.026
Good work.

17:50.110 --> 17:51.361
- You too.
- Thank you.

17:52.195 --> 17:53.196
So...

17:54.864 --> 17:56.032
you want to grab dinner?

17:57.284 --> 17:58.285
Okay.

17:58.994 --> 18:00.370
- It's hot. Be careful.
- Okay.

18:04.874 --> 18:05.875
What are you doing?

18:06.001 --> 18:07.669
This is Ui-yeong's tip.

18:07.752 --> 18:10.046
This way, you can eat quickly
without burning yourself.

18:15.385 --> 18:16.886
Gosh, you little piggy.

18:18.763 --> 18:19.764
She's so cute.

18:22.851 --> 18:24.019
- Like this?
- Yeah.

18:31.276 --> 18:32.277
I got this.

18:36.323 --> 18:38.283
It doesn't move when you even it out.

18:39.743 --> 18:40.785
See? It's stable.

18:44.706 --> 18:45.957
He's so cool.

18:49.252 --> 18:53.131
We won't let our relationship
affect our work.

18:53.214 --> 18:54.924
- Okay.
- You think you can do that?

18:55.467 --> 18:58.637
You two look great together.

18:58.720 --> 18:59.846
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

19:00.347 --> 19:02.432
We don't have to worry
about being caught anymore.

19:02.766 --> 19:06.311
We'll do all the tough things together
and work hard.

19:06.394 --> 19:07.395
Okay.

19:07.687 --> 19:09.564
- Should we get matching rings?
- Should we?

19:09.648 --> 19:11.983
Matching rings?
You're getting rings already?

19:12.108 --> 19:14.110
If we want, why not?

19:14.194 --> 19:17.197
But it's too soon.
You just started dating.

19:17.280 --> 19:18.782
Kids these days move fast.

19:19.616 --> 19:22.327
Wow, am I working
or watching a dating show?

19:23.244 --> 19:26.206
Poor Choi Bo-yoon,
she's so bitter and lonely.

19:26.456 --> 19:29.125
You're not the one to talk, okay?

19:29.209 --> 19:30.710
You're just as single as I am.

19:30.794 --> 19:32.003
Hey, I...

19:32.462 --> 19:34.381
You know what? You know nothing.

19:34.464 --> 19:37.092
I have my Sua, at least.

19:37.926 --> 19:39.552
Hello, my baby!

19:39.636 --> 19:40.887
- Dad.
- Yeah?

19:40.970 --> 19:43.515
We're having an early dismissal
because of a blackout.

19:43.598 --> 19:44.891
Should I pick you up, then?

19:44.974 --> 19:46.768
No, come after work.

19:46.851 --> 19:48.269
I'm hanging out with Min-gyu.

19:48.645 --> 19:50.146
Min-gyu? Who's that?

19:50.522 --> 19:52.691
My boyfriend. Did I not tell you?

19:53.191 --> 19:54.359
Your boyfriend?

19:57.362 --> 20:01.282
I told her to ask me for permission,
whether it's a guy friend or a boyfriend!

20:01.533 --> 20:04.202
Why is she already dating someone?
She's in kindergarten!

20:05.954 --> 20:08.790
Tae-seop's left me, and now, Jin-su.

20:08.957 --> 20:09.958
Sua!

20:12.001 --> 20:13.962
Oh, you must be Min-gyu.

20:14.045 --> 20:15.296
Hello.

20:15.380 --> 20:18.383
Good to know my Sua has good taste.

20:18.466 --> 20:19.551
Are you two alone?

20:21.136 --> 20:22.387
Mom!

20:45.160 --> 20:46.286
Alright!

20:46.369 --> 20:47.620
- Mom.
- Yeah?

20:47.704 --> 20:49.456
Sua's dad gave me soap bubbles.

20:49.539 --> 20:51.750
Really? Did you thank him?

20:52.083 --> 20:53.293
Go and thank him.

20:53.918 --> 20:55.670
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

20:56.212 --> 20:59.132
- Go and play with Sua.
- He was raised by good parents.

20:59.215 --> 21:00.258
Thank you.

21:00.341 --> 21:01.426
It's nothing.

21:02.469 --> 21:06.222
It's my first time hearing about Min-gyu.

21:07.640 --> 21:09.517
That's because we only recently moved here

21:09.601 --> 21:11.936
after my divorce from his dad.

21:12.020 --> 21:13.104
I see.

21:14.272 --> 21:15.857
Well, my wife's passed away.

21:17.233 --> 21:18.276
I see.

21:20.278 --> 21:24.783
I was worried about Min-gyu settling in
because he's so shy

21:25.992 --> 21:29.370
but I'm so glad
he got so close to Sua so quickly.

21:29.454 --> 21:32.624
Sua gets along with everyone.

21:32.832 --> 21:34.584
Let's be friends, too.

21:36.711 --> 21:38.004
Sure.

21:40.006 --> 21:41.841
Looks like they'll be here for a while.

21:41.925 --> 21:44.052
Do you want to have dinner nearby?

21:45.011 --> 21:46.721
I'm sure you don't want to cook at home.

21:49.224 --> 21:51.768
Oh, yeah, that's true, but...

21:52.435 --> 21:53.478
What about kalguksu?

21:55.104 --> 21:58.274
Do you like it?

22:00.026 --> 22:01.027
Yeah.

22:02.529 --> 22:04.030
I think I'll like it.

22:28.847 --> 22:30.473
- Hello.
- Hey.

22:31.391 --> 22:33.017
Is something going on upstairs?

22:33.226 --> 22:36.229
Ji-su's doing a magazine interview here.

22:37.272 --> 22:39.274
- That's great.
- But you can get coffee.

22:39.357 --> 22:41.901
We'll take two lattes for takeout.

22:41.985 --> 22:43.069
Okay.

22:43.361 --> 22:46.281
Should we go upstairs and watch for a bit
before we go?

22:47.323 --> 22:48.449
Can we do that?

22:48.533 --> 22:49.534
Of course.

22:50.159 --> 22:51.411
Should we do that, then?

22:51.619 --> 22:53.788
Could you say something
about Ms. Son Jeong-a

22:54.080 --> 22:57.041
who must be very special to you?

22:58.918 --> 23:02.297
Jeong-a was so charismatic on the set.

23:03.256 --> 23:06.009
I could feel her focus while acting

23:06.342 --> 23:08.261
and passion on the set very well.

23:08.344 --> 23:09.929
- He looks legit!
- I learned a lot.

23:10.013 --> 23:11.639
- If I get another chance
- Yeah.

23:11.723 --> 23:13.850
I'd love to work with her again.

23:14.976 --> 23:16.019
I see.

23:16.477 --> 23:19.355
What kind of actor do you want to become?

23:35.663 --> 23:37.248
Whatever it is

23:40.084 --> 23:42.253
don't try so hard to run from it.

23:43.463 --> 23:45.673
Use that time and effort

23:47.300 --> 23:49.510
to stand for what you love.

23:52.972 --> 23:54.807
I'm sure there are things you love.

23:57.810 --> 24:00.855
Do that for a day, a month, then a year.

24:02.106 --> 24:03.775
Keep it up

24:05.485 --> 24:09.072
and one day, you'll feel just fine.

24:18.289 --> 24:20.041
My friend once told me

24:22.293 --> 24:26.214
to stand for what I love.

24:31.010 --> 24:33.388
So, I looked deep inside myself

24:37.976 --> 24:39.936
and realized I loved acting.

24:42.105 --> 24:45.608
She really challenged
the way I used to think.

24:47.193 --> 24:49.529
Instead of setting a certain direction
for myself

24:50.113 --> 24:53.408
I want to focus on the present
and chase what makes my heart beat.

24:54.993 --> 24:56.911
- That's incredible.
- Should we get going?

24:57.328 --> 24:58.538
Yeah, let's go.

25:09.215 --> 25:11.884
So, I want to work
on a romance project next.

25:12.468 --> 25:14.595
I want it to be a happy, loving story.

25:16.222 --> 25:17.682
I want to find love in a role

25:17.765 --> 25:20.518
and live the life I couldn't live
in reality.

25:20.643 --> 25:22.687
- I hope you get that role.
- Thanks.

25:31.237 --> 25:32.947
Ji-su's so amazing.

25:33.573 --> 25:34.907
He is.

25:36.951 --> 25:37.952
Alright.

25:43.624 --> 25:45.334
If everyone's free this weekend

25:45.418 --> 25:47.754
why don't we have an Eat Eat Club meeting
this weekend?

25:47.837 --> 25:49.130
I have something to say.

25:49.630 --> 25:50.715
Sounds good!

25:51.466 --> 25:52.717
Sounds good!

25:58.097 --> 25:59.557
I have something to tell you.

26:00.058 --> 26:01.100
What is it?

26:01.184 --> 26:03.436
I'm moving in with Jun.

26:03.519 --> 26:05.855
Huh? You two are...

26:06.898 --> 26:07.899
moving in together?

26:09.650 --> 26:11.903
He was tight on money
with the gym rent being raised

26:11.986 --> 26:15.323
so I told him to move in with me
with just his toothbrush.

26:15.448 --> 26:17.617
It took him a few days to think about it

26:17.909 --> 26:19.202
but he eventually said yes.

26:19.744 --> 26:22.747
Hold up. Isn't it too soon?

26:23.331 --> 26:24.832
Wouldn't you feel uncomfortable?

26:25.041 --> 26:28.961
It's fine. He comes home late
and just sleeps all day.

26:29.045 --> 26:31.589
And we were always compatible...

26:34.383 --> 26:35.802
in bed, anyway.

26:38.221 --> 26:39.764
Are you really sure?

26:41.057 --> 26:45.019
I didn't give it a lot of thought
before going ahead with it.

26:45.103 --> 26:46.979
I just felt bad for him.

26:47.313 --> 26:49.357
It's not because he's my boyfriend.

26:49.732 --> 26:53.653
I've just never seen anyone
so earnest and hardworking.

26:54.612 --> 26:55.947
I see your point.

26:56.030 --> 26:58.116
Life is so tough

26:58.366 --> 27:01.953
so I want to be my Jun's lucky charm.

27:04.705 --> 27:06.457
You've changed.

27:07.291 --> 27:09.001
You've gotten more serious.

27:10.545 --> 27:12.255
Or should I say you grew up?

27:13.047 --> 27:14.423
- Really?
- Yeah.

27:16.843 --> 27:18.845
I already have a mature body!

27:18.928 --> 27:21.430
It's too dangerous
if I actually become mature, too.

27:22.056 --> 27:23.766
- Aren't I right?
- My gosh.

27:24.600 --> 27:25.852
I take back what I just said.

27:25.935 --> 27:26.978
Forget I ever said that.

27:29.689 --> 27:32.692
I should ask if I can invite Jun
to the Eat Eat Club, too.

27:33.151 --> 27:34.694
- You're okay with it, right?
- Yeah.

27:34.861 --> 27:35.862
Sounds fine with me.

27:35.945 --> 27:38.364
He's family now.
I have to make sure he eats well.

27:38.447 --> 27:41.409
- Already?
- Ui-yeong!

27:41.742 --> 27:43.452
Can we have a word? And Hyun-min, too.

27:43.536 --> 27:45.788
- Okay.
- Okay.

27:49.208 --> 27:51.586
- About the fruit shipment yesterday.
- Yes?

27:51.669 --> 27:53.754
The quality is too inconsistent.

27:54.172 --> 27:57.466
The Restaurant Department just complained,
saying they couldn't cook with them.

27:57.758 --> 27:59.760
Every box tastes different.

27:59.844 --> 28:02.263
Have you not been managing our suppliers
while I was gone?

28:02.346 --> 28:05.057
We checked them when we received them.

28:05.141 --> 28:07.977
You should've done a better job, then.

28:08.060 --> 28:11.105
Are you going to do a half-assed job
with everything now?

28:12.440 --> 28:14.901
Didn't we get yesterday's shipment
from K Fruits?

28:16.110 --> 28:18.404
You were the one who signed with them...

28:19.488 --> 28:20.823
Stop it.

28:21.240 --> 28:25.036
Can you just make sure
we don't have more issues?

28:25.995 --> 28:27.663
Where's Na-ri?

28:33.961 --> 28:35.546
I had to check some docs.

28:35.630 --> 28:37.131
Regarding the fruit complaint.

28:37.215 --> 28:40.760
Yeah, I was just warning them right now.

28:41.260 --> 28:42.303
You were the one

28:42.595 --> 28:44.680
who recommended that supplier.

28:44.764 --> 28:46.682
You did the site visit by yourself, too.

28:46.766 --> 28:49.060
You're the one who messed up
with this supplier

28:49.143 --> 28:51.562
so why are you scolding
our innocent employees?

28:52.772 --> 28:53.981
What did you say?

28:54.899 --> 28:57.318
What do you mean that I signed them?

28:58.027 --> 28:59.362
Oh, yeah, I visited them.

28:59.946 --> 29:02.990
Ui-yeong, it was a part of the contract
to check the quality

29:03.074 --> 29:06.827
so return the whole shipment to K Fruits
and make another order.

29:07.161 --> 29:12.041
Oh, and tell them we'll cut ties with them
if they mess up like this again.

29:12.667 --> 29:14.126
Okay, got it.

29:15.670 --> 29:17.046
Okay, that's sorted.

29:17.129 --> 29:20.466
But I heard you agreed to Marketing
moving up the new menu release

29:20.549 --> 29:22.843
without consulting us.

29:22.927 --> 29:25.429
- We were...
- Shouldn't you have discussed it

29:25.513 --> 29:28.432
with your team first
before going forward with it?

29:28.891 --> 29:32.061
We don't appreciate the way you do things.

29:32.144 --> 29:35.856
We worked tirelessly to cover for you
while you were gone.

29:35.940 --> 29:38.359
But we realized

29:38.734 --> 29:40.528
your absence didn't affect us much.

29:41.404 --> 29:43.406
With Ui-yeong, in particular.

29:54.333 --> 29:57.295
Are you here as my interior designer
or as a customer?

29:59.005 --> 30:01.132
About these rings...

30:01.549 --> 30:03.676
Could you make them one more time?

30:05.261 --> 30:07.471
- For you and your girlfriend?
- Yeah.

30:12.310 --> 30:15.062
Sure, I can make a special exception
just for you.

30:17.023 --> 30:19.066
Do you know your girlfriend's ring size?

30:20.067 --> 30:22.403
I'm not really sure. What do I do?

30:22.486 --> 30:25.364
You can ask for her ring size
or bring a ring she wears.

30:25.448 --> 30:27.700
Oh, yeah, she wears a lot of rings.

30:28.242 --> 30:29.744
Should I steal one from her?

30:31.245 --> 30:34.206
I can't work on the rings for a while
once you start the renovation

30:34.457 --> 30:35.499
so hurry.

30:35.583 --> 30:37.001
Okay, thank you.

30:45.551 --> 30:46.802
So, that's how it's done.

30:49.555 --> 30:50.681
I love that guy.

30:53.851 --> 30:54.894
I'm hungry.

30:57.480 --> 30:58.814
That's so cool.

31:08.991 --> 31:10.659
Let's go there one day, okay?

31:11.911 --> 31:12.912
Let's go there.

31:13.496 --> 31:15.956
Yeah, I wanted to go, too.

31:20.669 --> 31:21.796
So, that's how they do it.

31:21.879 --> 31:23.214
- Just a sec.
- Okay.

31:26.592 --> 31:28.135
Oh, hi, Mr. Eun.

31:28.594 --> 31:30.304
- Hey, Ui-yeong.
- Hi.

31:30.388 --> 31:32.348
Sorry for calling you so late.

31:32.431 --> 31:33.432
It's okay.

31:33.516 --> 31:36.811
You know your friend
who's getting married next week?

31:36.894 --> 31:39.021
- Yeah, Eun-mi?
- Yes.

31:39.105 --> 31:42.274
The manager in charge of the event
just got a call

31:42.358 --> 31:45.736
asking how much it'd cost
to cancel the wedding now.

31:45.820 --> 31:48.322
Did she? And did she cancel it?

31:48.406 --> 31:49.532
No.

31:49.657 --> 31:52.785
She was surprised by how much it'd cost
and hung up.

31:53.244 --> 31:56.705
But she didn't sound like she was okay

31:56.914 --> 31:58.999
so I thought I should tell you.

31:59.834 --> 32:02.586
Okay, thank you.

32:04.588 --> 32:06.632
What's wrong?
Something wrong with your finger...

32:07.341 --> 32:09.009
No, something wrong with your friend?

32:09.552 --> 32:12.721
She asked if she could cancel the wedding.

32:12.805 --> 32:13.806
Hmm?

32:14.140 --> 32:16.475
- I'd better call her.
- Yeah.

32:18.519 --> 32:19.562
What's going on?

32:30.030 --> 32:31.282
- Hello.
- Hello.

32:31.365 --> 32:33.451
- Who's the reservation for?
- Lee Eun-mi.

32:33.534 --> 32:35.035
- Oh, come this way.
- Okay.

32:42.251 --> 32:43.919
It's the dress for your wedding, right?

32:44.753 --> 32:46.213
You chose a great one!

32:46.297 --> 32:47.673
It suits you so well.

32:47.756 --> 32:49.592
I'll get it ready
so that you can try it on.

32:49.758 --> 32:53.053
Oh, I'm not the bride. It's my friend.

32:53.929 --> 32:55.890
- Oh, sorry!
- It's okay.

32:55.973 --> 32:58.476
Brides usually come alone
on the last fitting day.

32:59.101 --> 33:00.811
Please sit and wait here.

33:00.895 --> 33:02.021
Okay, thank you.

33:11.780 --> 33:15.326
I just wanted to check
how much the cancellation would be.

33:17.536 --> 33:20.080
You sure nothing's wrong?

33:20.164 --> 33:21.916
No, everything's fine.

33:22.458 --> 33:25.127
I just thought
I was supposed to get married by now.

33:25.586 --> 33:29.256
And I know it's not easy to find a guy
who checks all the boxes like my fiancé.

33:30.466 --> 33:32.801
But I don't know why I'm so nervous.

33:33.302 --> 33:37.264
I'm really not sure if this is the man
I should commit the rest of my life to.

33:40.726 --> 33:45.356
You must be feeling overwhelmed
with the wedding coming up so soon

33:45.940 --> 33:50.027
but I hear it's common to get
that "marriage blues."

33:56.700 --> 33:59.787
Eun-mi, you look stunning.

34:07.336 --> 34:09.880
Yeah, I lost so much weight for this.

34:10.047 --> 34:11.382
And spent so much money.

34:12.216 --> 34:14.385
I can't cancel the wedding
after inviting everyone.

34:14.927 --> 34:16.762
I'd even embarrass my parents.

34:18.472 --> 34:19.640
I have to go ahead with it.

34:23.018 --> 34:24.061
It looks great.

34:24.228 --> 34:25.354
Yeah, it's beautiful.

34:31.443 --> 34:33.487
Do you really have to get divorced?

34:33.654 --> 34:35.447
Are you sure you won't change your mind?

34:35.823 --> 34:37.199
Yeah, I'm sure of it.

34:37.533 --> 34:40.452
We don't have a lot of time left to live.
Let's enjoy it in peace.

34:41.287 --> 34:42.288
Fine.

34:42.955 --> 34:44.415
See you at the court next week.

34:55.759 --> 34:57.052
ORGANIC FERTILIZER

34:57.136 --> 34:59.346
- I'm home!
- Hey.

34:59.430 --> 35:01.974
What are you doing? Repotting the plants?

35:02.057 --> 35:04.393
Yeah, I've been putting it off
for a while.

35:05.311 --> 35:08.689
I thought this was fully grown
because it stopped growing.

35:08.772 --> 35:09.773
Oh.

35:10.232 --> 35:13.694
It stopped growing because the roots had
no more space to expand into.

35:14.320 --> 35:17.406
It realized that this was
as tall as it could become in this pot.

35:18.699 --> 35:21.994
- Do you want me to help?
- No, you'll get dirt on your clothes.

35:22.494 --> 35:24.496
Right. Your dad texted me.

35:25.456 --> 35:27.791
Yeah? What did he say?

35:28.167 --> 35:29.793
He agreed to getting divorced.

35:32.171 --> 35:34.340
We're meeting at court next week.

35:37.259 --> 35:39.803
Okay, I'll keep that in mind.

35:40.095 --> 35:41.096
Okay.

36:00.407 --> 36:03.243
SPEECH FOR THE WEDDING TOAST

36:06.413 --> 36:08.415
In the fairy tales I read as a kid,

36:08.499 --> 36:10.459
marriage was
the definition of a happy ending.

36:11.877 --> 36:14.171
But now that I'm older

36:14.880 --> 36:16.965
I completely understand my friend's fear

36:17.049 --> 36:19.510
at the thought of spending her life
with one man.

36:20.636 --> 36:21.804
And my mom's divorce looks

36:22.346 --> 36:25.307
like a happy ending
where she gets her life back.

36:27.017 --> 36:31.438
So, why do people choose to get married?

36:37.778 --> 36:38.946
Hello

36:39.029 --> 36:42.491
I'm Lee Ui-yeong,
a friend of the bride, Eun-mi.

36:43.242 --> 36:46.870
It's a huge honor to join
the lovely couple today

36:48.330 --> 36:49.790
in their most precious moment.

36:50.833 --> 36:53.293
For the two to get here...

36:56.880 --> 36:59.675
What brings you here out of the blue?
You should've come in.

37:00.175 --> 37:02.678
Aren't you joining us
for the Eat Eat Club meeting today?

37:02.928 --> 37:05.723
I wanted to ask you something before that.

37:06.390 --> 37:07.391
Huh?

37:11.520 --> 37:14.940
So, you want to surprise her with a ring

37:15.274 --> 37:17.151
- but don't know her size?
- No.

37:17.776 --> 37:20.738
I tried to measure her finger
without her knowing, but it wasn't easy.

37:21.155 --> 37:24.783
Could you casually ask her for me
without her noticing anything?

37:27.828 --> 37:31.248
Are you trying to do
what the young ones do these days

37:31.331 --> 37:33.333
and propose to her?

37:33.417 --> 37:35.127
No, it's not like that.

37:35.210 --> 37:38.172
Why not? Isn't it about time
you think about getting married?

37:39.840 --> 37:41.717
I'm always open to it

37:41.800 --> 37:43.635
but it's not something I can do alone.

37:44.428 --> 37:48.307
I'm just waiting for Ui-yeong
to become interested in it.

37:48.390 --> 37:49.641
Don't worry, I got you.

37:49.725 --> 37:52.853
I'm the Cupid for you two. Just trust me.

37:52.978 --> 37:55.856
I'll get those rings
on both of your fingers.

37:56.482 --> 37:57.483
Okay.

38:07.409 --> 38:09.244
- Eat up.
- Could I have some soup?

38:09.328 --> 38:11.121
This is milt. It's a specialty.

38:11.830 --> 38:13.791
I'll mix the drinks my way.

38:13.874 --> 38:15.959
Oh, yeah, drinks! Tae-seop!

38:16.168 --> 38:17.169
Oh, right.

38:17.252 --> 38:19.630
My mom's taking care
of the drinks tonight.

38:19.713 --> 38:21.089
Drink whatever you want.

38:21.173 --> 38:22.341
The owner said it was okay.

38:22.883 --> 38:24.468
- Those are some good ones.
- Yeah.

38:24.551 --> 38:26.762
- Should we start with the expensive one?
- Right on!

38:26.845 --> 38:28.722
- I'll pour them into soju glasses.
- Okay.

38:28.806 --> 38:31.016
- Please thank your mom for us.
- Okay.

38:31.099 --> 38:34.061
My mom's trying to get healthy.

38:34.228 --> 38:35.604
With that said, Seung-jun

38:35.687 --> 38:38.065
sign my mom and me up
for ten personal trainer sessions.

38:38.440 --> 38:39.441
- Really?
- Yeah.

38:39.525 --> 38:40.692
I'll take 20 classes, then.

38:41.151 --> 38:43.070
- It'll be fun to work out together.
- Yeah!

38:44.655 --> 38:45.823
- Thank you.
- It's nothing.

38:45.906 --> 38:48.242
I'll give all of you
three extra sessions, then.

38:48.325 --> 38:49.827
Right on!

38:50.702 --> 38:52.621
Is Sae-byeok not coming?

38:52.704 --> 38:55.707
She had tickets to a show,
and couldn't cancel it.

38:55.791 --> 38:58.669
I guess she's busy dating her colleague!

38:58.752 --> 39:00.045
- So cute.
- Really?

39:00.170 --> 39:02.464
I wanted to break the news
with everyone around.

39:03.966 --> 39:07.845
I'm quitting at the hotel soon
and leaving the country.

39:08.387 --> 39:10.430
That's so sudden.

39:10.556 --> 39:11.932
Where are you going?

39:12.015 --> 39:15.227
I've been offered the Head Chef position
at a fusion restaurant in New York.

39:16.812 --> 39:19.398
I thought I'd announce it
before we started eating.

39:20.566 --> 39:21.984
Congratulations!

39:22.067 --> 39:23.068
Congratulations.

39:23.151 --> 39:24.695
- Thank you.
- Congratulations!

39:24.778 --> 39:26.572
But could you stay with us a bit longer?

39:27.364 --> 39:28.740
- Mr. Eun!
- Yeah?

39:28.824 --> 39:31.201
How can you let
such a talented chef leave?

39:31.285 --> 39:34.079
If that's what she wants, what can I do?

39:34.162 --> 39:37.040
Chefs never stay at a place
for all that long.

39:37.124 --> 39:39.626
We always move to another place
where we can improve.

39:40.586 --> 39:43.505
But thanks to you,
I got to try chicken feet

39:44.631 --> 39:46.717
gaebul, sundae

39:46.800 --> 39:48.302
and now, fresh daegu-tang.

39:48.594 --> 39:50.053
This was a huge inspiration.

39:50.846 --> 39:54.224
I'm glad the Eat Eat Club took a part
in your growth.

39:54.892 --> 39:56.560
Alright, let's dig in.

39:57.019 --> 39:59.688
- Cheers! Congrats!
- Congrats!

39:59.771 --> 40:01.315
- Congrats!
- It's on me today.

40:01.398 --> 40:02.733
- Really?
- My gosh!

40:02.816 --> 40:04.902
- Thank you.
- Thank you!

40:05.986 --> 40:09.990
I can't believe
Westerners only deep-fry cod.

40:12.701 --> 40:14.202
The broth is perfect!

40:14.286 --> 40:16.997
You can't forget about us
once you taste it.

40:17.080 --> 40:19.333
Not at all. I can't forget this.

40:19.416 --> 40:20.500
It's good, right?

40:25.047 --> 40:28.467
Since we're all here,
I also have a question for everyone.

40:28.550 --> 40:29.718
What is it?

40:30.427 --> 40:35.849
I want to get a ring for my wife.

40:37.392 --> 40:39.478
What's your ring size, Ui-yeong?

40:39.561 --> 40:40.562
Me?

40:42.314 --> 40:46.777
Why are you asking Ui-yeong
when it's for your wife?

40:48.654 --> 40:49.655
Hmm?

40:51.740 --> 40:54.242
Her hands are as big as Ui-yeong's.

40:54.326 --> 40:55.619
Oh, really?

40:56.078 --> 40:57.996
- My size is...
- Yeah?

41:01.708 --> 41:02.751
I have no idea.

41:03.168 --> 41:05.087
I don't think anyone knows their size.
Do you?

41:05.212 --> 41:06.213
A small?

41:06.672 --> 41:07.881
I guess I'd be an x-small.

41:08.840 --> 41:10.217
I don't know it, either.

41:10.467 --> 41:11.510
I see.

41:11.927 --> 41:13.303
- Sorry.
- It's okay.

41:13.387 --> 41:14.972
Gosh, what should I do now?

41:16.098 --> 41:19.893
I thought you'd know
your wife's ring size.

41:19.977 --> 41:21.687
Since you're always so good to her.

41:21.895 --> 41:23.855
Honey, remember mine from now on.

41:23.939 --> 41:25.107
Check my left ring finger.

41:26.108 --> 41:27.943
- Thank you.
- Take the ring.

41:28.402 --> 41:29.486
Thank you.

41:30.195 --> 41:33.824
Gosh, I'm a huge disappointment today.

41:35.575 --> 41:36.785
My gosh.

41:37.953 --> 41:40.122
I don't know why I want soju

41:41.373 --> 41:42.958
with all these expensive drinks here.

41:43.750 --> 41:44.751
Man!

41:46.253 --> 41:48.088
Should I pour you a glass?

41:48.171 --> 41:49.172
Sure.

41:50.632 --> 41:52.092
- Oh, my!
- Slow down.

42:07.149 --> 42:08.150
Ui-yeong

42:08.775 --> 42:12.529
I'm going back home
after filing my divorce at the court

42:12.821 --> 42:13.905
with your mom.

42:15.365 --> 42:17.659
Sorry for causing you so much trouble.

42:18.493 --> 42:20.829
Let's meet up once things are sorted.

42:28.128 --> 42:30.797
SONGI SPICY CHICKEN FEET

42:42.559 --> 42:44.186
Rice balls? Okay!

42:46.021 --> 42:47.064
Hello!

42:47.147 --> 42:48.398
Can I get takeout?

42:48.482 --> 42:49.691
Of course!

42:49.775 --> 42:51.234
How many people is it for?

42:51.318 --> 42:52.319
- Two.
- Two?

42:52.402 --> 42:54.237
I'll prepare a medium, then.

42:54.321 --> 42:55.572
I have a takeout order!

42:55.655 --> 42:57.741
Feel free to wait upstairs.

42:57.824 --> 42:59.409
- I'll bring it right to you.
- Okay.

42:59.618 --> 43:01.453
Honey, a medium for takeout!

43:01.536 --> 43:02.829
SEOUL FAMILY COURT

43:06.249 --> 43:08.376
Here are your rice balls.

43:09.294 --> 43:11.421
BELOVED TREASURE
WE'RE ALL A TREASURE TO SOMEONE

43:16.301 --> 43:19.096
- My son hung that up for us.
- I see.

43:19.304 --> 43:22.099
You know how we forget
about how precious we are

43:22.182 --> 43:23.391
when life gets crazy.

43:23.475 --> 43:25.310
I wanted my customers to remember it

43:25.560 --> 43:27.646
at least when they were eating
their chicken feet.

43:28.063 --> 43:29.439
This is on the house.

43:29.523 --> 43:31.399
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

43:32.275 --> 43:35.153
But I feel like your son wrote it

43:35.570 --> 43:38.365
as a reminder to all your customers
that they should respect you

43:38.448 --> 43:40.492
because you're precious.

43:42.994 --> 43:44.079
You think so?

43:45.872 --> 43:50.794
Well, I guess my son is
the most thoughtful person ever.

43:51.920 --> 43:54.381
By the way,
it's your first time here, right?

43:54.464 --> 43:55.841
Yeah, it's my first time

43:55.924 --> 43:57.968
but my daughter loves
the chicken feet here.

43:58.051 --> 44:00.512
- Your daughter must be a regular!
- Yeah.

44:01.012 --> 44:04.349
She has good taste, you know?

44:04.432 --> 44:05.433
I see.

44:05.517 --> 44:07.561
She has a keen eye

44:07.644 --> 44:09.646
for good ingredients and flavors in food.

44:09.938 --> 44:11.231
Hold on.

44:11.690 --> 44:16.069
I know most of my regulars.

44:16.611 --> 44:18.321
Oh, now that I think about it

44:18.405 --> 44:23.493
the way your lips curve when you smile...

44:23.743 --> 44:26.121
Just kidding, I hvae no idea.

44:28.582 --> 44:30.125
I'll come with her next time.

44:30.208 --> 44:33.545
Sure, come with her

44:33.628 --> 44:37.007
and I'll give you
steamed eggs and rice on the house.

44:37.090 --> 44:39.050
- Okay, thank you.
- I'll bring your food soon.

44:39.134 --> 44:40.302
Thank you.

44:43.013 --> 44:44.014
I can't wait to try it.

44:46.224 --> 44:48.935
Oh, your parents went to court today.

44:49.477 --> 44:50.687
Yeah.

44:51.563 --> 44:53.064
I thought about going with Mom

44:53.481 --> 44:56.234
but it seemed
like they wanted to end things peacefully.

44:56.943 --> 44:57.986
Good choice.

44:58.069 --> 44:59.863
Tae-seop, you know the chair?

45:00.238 --> 45:02.365
- I'm sitting in it right now.
- Okay.

45:02.449 --> 45:03.950
What's wrong? Is it uncomfortable?

45:04.284 --> 45:06.494
No, it's the opposite.

45:06.953 --> 45:10.373
See how I'm talking
about my parents' divorce so peacefully?

45:11.875 --> 45:12.918
Well

45:13.543 --> 45:15.295
there's a secret to it.

45:15.378 --> 45:16.463
What is it?

45:16.546 --> 45:20.300
The back panel leans back
at seven degrees.

45:20.759 --> 45:22.802
That tiny change makes it
so comfortable, right?

45:23.595 --> 45:25.055
Yeah, it's the best.

45:25.764 --> 45:29.100
I always have your back, too

45:29.601 --> 45:30.936
so lean on me anytime.

45:31.686 --> 45:32.729
Okay.

45:33.521 --> 45:34.898
Oh, my mom's home.

45:34.981 --> 45:36.566
- I'll call you later.
- Okay.

45:37.275 --> 45:39.277
- Hey, Mom.
- Hey.

45:40.111 --> 45:41.112
What's that?

45:41.279 --> 45:42.864
- You haven't had dinner, right?
- No.

45:43.156 --> 45:44.449
- I got your favorite.
- What?

45:44.532 --> 45:45.575
SONGI SPICY CHICKEN FEET

45:46.451 --> 45:48.119
- Songi Spicy Chicken Feet?
- Yeah.

45:53.458 --> 45:56.878
So, the owner that I met today is
Tae-seop's mom?

45:56.962 --> 46:00.257
Yeah! I was so surprised
when I first found out.

46:00.340 --> 46:01.341
Small world, huh?

46:03.093 --> 46:06.221
- Does kindness run in the family?
- What?

46:06.596 --> 46:09.724
She gave me a can of soda on the house
when I was waiting for the food.

46:10.225 --> 46:11.977
- Did she?
- Yeah.

46:20.485 --> 46:21.778
Mom

46:22.279 --> 46:24.406
did everything go smoothly at the court?

46:25.532 --> 46:26.533
Yeah.

46:27.659 --> 46:29.577
Nothing happened. It was quick.

46:30.495 --> 46:32.664
Oh, we have to be back in a month.

46:33.540 --> 46:36.668
I feel so liberated now.
I don't know why I took so long.

46:40.005 --> 46:41.715
- Mom
- Hmm?

46:42.299 --> 46:45.302
you wouldn't get married
if you could go back in time, right?

46:47.971 --> 46:49.264
I think I'd still do it.

46:49.347 --> 46:50.432
You would?

46:51.141 --> 46:54.144
Sure, we separated in the end

46:54.477 --> 46:58.440
but that was the best choice I could make
in that point in life.

46:58.648 --> 47:02.068
So, even if I were to go back,
I'd probably choose the same.

47:03.778 --> 47:06.239
What if you went back in time
with these memories?

47:06.656 --> 47:08.783
People think about this all the time.

47:09.284 --> 47:11.786
I'd try even harder to make
the exact same choices, then.

47:11.870 --> 47:13.455
So I can meet you again.

47:14.122 --> 47:16.958
What? Just to bring me into the world?

47:17.042 --> 47:19.169
Yeah, as wild as life gets

47:19.544 --> 47:21.379
being alive is fun.

47:22.213 --> 47:25.050
And I feel less lonely with you.

47:30.055 --> 47:32.307
Maybe I should take days off at work

47:32.724 --> 47:34.726
and enjoy my freedom on a trip.

47:35.310 --> 47:36.978
Maybe learn a new language, too.

47:37.062 --> 47:40.523
I've always wanted to learn Spanish.

47:41.358 --> 47:42.609
Should we go together?

47:42.692 --> 47:45.779
Should we get a savings account
to save for trips?

47:45.862 --> 47:47.405
- That's a great idea!
- Right?

47:47.864 --> 47:49.282
You can pay for 70% of it.

47:49.366 --> 47:52.202
I swear you're an evil stepmom.

48:12.013 --> 48:13.515
How do I look? Do I look okay?

48:13.598 --> 48:16.226
"Okay"? You look like an angel!

48:17.519 --> 48:20.021
I made sure to warm up my lips
for that speech.

48:20.355 --> 48:23.775
Make sure to stretch your facial muscles
because you're about to laugh nonstop.

48:26.528 --> 48:29.823
- Hey!
- Hey, you're here!

48:29.906 --> 48:32.242
- Come and take photos.
- Come and sit.

48:36.371 --> 48:38.164
- The main character.
- Ta-da!

48:38.915 --> 48:40.166
I feel so nervous.

48:43.837 --> 48:46.297
GUESTS FOR THE BRIDE

48:46.381 --> 48:48.258
I've heard a lot about you.

48:48.341 --> 48:49.884
Thank you.

48:49.968 --> 48:51.761
- Hello.
- Congratulations.

48:51.845 --> 48:53.471
- Thank you!
- He grew up so much!

48:53.555 --> 48:56.349
- My goodness!
- I haven't seen you in forever.

48:56.433 --> 48:59.144
- Don't they look so happy?
- The dress looks perfect on her!

48:59.227 --> 49:00.562
- She looks amazing.
- Right?

49:00.645 --> 49:02.897
- She looks like a princess.
- She looks so happy.

49:02.981 --> 49:04.107
- Right?
- Inspired yet?

49:04.190 --> 49:05.942
- Come on.
- Stop it.

49:07.193 --> 49:08.361
- I know.
- Ui-yeong.

49:08.445 --> 49:09.571
Oh, hi.

49:09.904 --> 49:10.947
That's my boyfriend.

49:11.614 --> 49:12.907
- Ui-yeong!
- No way!

49:12.991 --> 49:14.659
- He's so handsome!
- You think so?

49:14.742 --> 49:15.994
You met him on a blind date?

49:16.077 --> 49:17.912
How did you get a man like that?

49:17.996 --> 49:19.747
Say hi to my friends.

49:19.831 --> 49:21.249
Hello, I'm Song Tae-seop.

49:21.332 --> 49:22.459
- Hello.
- Hello.

49:22.542 --> 49:24.085
We're her friends from college.

49:24.169 --> 49:25.837
Yeah, she's told me a lot about you.

49:25.920 --> 49:27.338
Really?

49:27.547 --> 49:29.883
- You two look great together.
- Really?

49:29.966 --> 49:32.302
Let's go on double dates sometime.

49:32.385 --> 49:34.012
Sure, invite me anytime.

49:34.095 --> 49:35.138
Okay!

49:35.221 --> 49:36.890
- The wedding is about to begin.
- Let's go.

49:36.973 --> 49:38.683
- Should we head in?
- Yeah.

49:38.766 --> 49:39.851
- We'll go.
- See you!

49:39.934 --> 49:41.311
- See you.
- Bye.

49:41.978 --> 49:43.730
He's so handsome!

49:43.813 --> 49:45.356
Excuse me!

49:45.773 --> 49:47.358
You're a friend of the bride, right?

49:47.442 --> 49:50.862
Yes, is something wrong?

49:52.238 --> 49:53.531
The bride...

49:53.948 --> 49:55.283
won't come out.

49:55.825 --> 49:56.910
Sorry?

49:57.202 --> 49:58.828
She won't come out.

49:59.537 --> 50:00.538
Oh...

50:02.707 --> 50:03.917
This way.

50:04.000 --> 50:06.753
BRIDE'S WAITING ROOM

50:06.961 --> 50:08.004
Here.

50:08.213 --> 50:10.590
She wanted to be left alone for a bit,
so I left her

50:10.673 --> 50:13.259
but now, she's locked the door
and won't even answer.

50:13.760 --> 50:15.929
Should I ask the venue manager
for the key?

50:17.222 --> 50:20.350
No, I'll try talking to her.

50:20.433 --> 50:21.434
Okay.

50:23.895 --> 50:25.897
I'll wait outside.

50:25.980 --> 50:27.023
Okay.

50:33.738 --> 50:36.074
Eun-mi, it's me.

50:39.077 --> 50:41.287
- Ui-yeong?
- Yeah.

50:41.621 --> 50:43.831
Are you okay? Are you not feeling well?

50:44.666 --> 50:47.418
My heart is beating too fast.
I feel like throwing up.

50:48.002 --> 50:49.879
And the dress is so suffocating.

50:50.964 --> 50:52.465
I did some research

50:52.632 --> 50:56.135
and it's still better to break up
and pay the penalty before the wedding.

50:56.594 --> 50:58.930
Eun-mi

50:59.013 --> 51:01.015
don't think about anything for now.

51:01.432 --> 51:03.685
Can you just open the door for me?

51:04.352 --> 51:05.603
I'm alone.

51:09.899 --> 51:10.984
Come on, Eun-mi.

51:15.363 --> 51:16.364
Eun-mi...

51:19.617 --> 51:20.785
It's okay.

51:21.995 --> 51:25.164
It's natural to feel nervous and scared.

51:27.083 --> 51:28.251
But...

51:29.294 --> 51:31.087
being scared of getting married

51:31.921 --> 51:35.967
and being unsure about the man himself
are different things.

51:38.386 --> 51:42.640
Did he really never feel
like he was the one?

51:51.983 --> 51:53.026
Ho-jin...

51:55.111 --> 51:56.362
Are you okay, Eun-mi?

51:56.738 --> 51:59.699
We really have to go now.

52:00.325 --> 52:01.367
It's okay.

52:01.784 --> 52:03.870
Being a little late isn't a big deal.

52:05.371 --> 52:06.414
Okay.

52:12.170 --> 52:13.296
I know it's been a lot.

52:21.095 --> 52:22.972
You've been in an uncomfortable dress
all day

52:23.681 --> 52:25.224
pretending to be completely fine.

52:26.434 --> 52:27.477
Eun-mi

52:27.894 --> 52:30.605
you don't have to go into the hall
if it's too much. It's fine.

52:33.107 --> 52:34.150
Ho-jin...

52:34.734 --> 52:35.818
It's okay.

52:37.445 --> 52:39.405
I'll always be by your side.

52:42.867 --> 52:43.910
Okay?

52:54.962 --> 52:56.631
I'm ready to go in.

52:59.217 --> 53:00.426
I'm ready.

53:05.056 --> 53:07.975
Hello, I'm the host of today's ceremony

53:08.059 --> 53:11.479
and the groom's friend, Yoo Jeong-hwa.

53:12.313 --> 53:15.566
On behalf of the bride and the groom

53:15.650 --> 53:18.403
as well as their families

53:18.486 --> 53:20.530
- What's wrong?
- thank you to everyone

53:20.613 --> 53:22.740
- for making time in your busy day.
- My speech is

53:22.824 --> 53:24.367
too oblivious.

53:24.784 --> 53:26.661
It's too happy.

53:28.371 --> 53:31.457
Just wing it, then.

53:31.541 --> 53:34.585
Whatever will be helpful,
as long as it's from your heart.

53:34.669 --> 53:37.547
Let's now begin
Jung Ho-jin and Lee Eun-mi's wedding.

53:38.047 --> 53:41.092
Please look to the back.

53:41.175 --> 53:45.930
The bride and the groom will now enter
in your blessing.

53:46.013 --> 53:48.891
Bride and groom, please enter.

53:51.602 --> 53:55.732
Please give them a big applause
to wish them a bright future.

53:58.317 --> 54:01.696
Friends, please cheer harder for them.

54:02.739 --> 54:05.700
The two are holding hands

54:05.783 --> 54:10.204
and calmly walking
toward a future together.

54:10.496 --> 54:13.082
You have taken your wedding vows

54:13.166 --> 54:16.961
to be with each other forevermore.

54:17.170 --> 54:18.921
This is a vow

54:19.005 --> 54:21.048
to love and cherish each other

54:21.549 --> 54:23.676
in sickness and in health

54:23.760 --> 54:26.471
in sadness and in joy

54:26.763 --> 54:28.014
and in every circumstance.

54:28.097 --> 54:32.602
Now, we will hear a wedding toast
from the bride's friend.

54:33.144 --> 54:34.228
Here I go.

54:48.493 --> 54:50.286
HELLO, I'M LEE UI-YEONG,
A FRIEND OF THE BRIDE, EUN-MI

55:00.129 --> 55:01.255
Hello

55:01.631 --> 55:04.008
I'm the friend's bride...

55:07.053 --> 55:09.722
The bride's friend, Lee Ui-yeong.

55:14.894 --> 55:17.355
I'm incredibly nervous right now

55:18.105 --> 55:21.192
but I know the bride and the groom
standing in front of me

55:21.275 --> 55:24.487
must be so much more nervous.

55:24.987 --> 55:28.157
In fact, they might feel
like their lives will flip upside-down

55:29.116 --> 55:34.038
by the time they leave the hall
after the wedding.

55:34.330 --> 55:36.123
THIRD ACT COMPANY ACTOR MEETING

55:36.207 --> 55:38.167
Take your time to read it, Ji-su.

55:38.251 --> 55:39.252
Okay.

55:39.669 --> 55:42.004
THIRD ACT COMPANY ACTOR CONTRACT

55:42.463 --> 55:46.467
We become hesitant
before making a big choice

55:46.968 --> 55:48.886
because we have no idea

55:49.554 --> 55:51.347
where our choice today

55:51.931 --> 55:53.683
will lead us to in the future.

55:53.766 --> 55:56.269
ACTOR SHIN JI-SU

56:05.820 --> 56:07.321
We don't know what doors will open

56:08.155 --> 56:10.908
and what doors will close.

56:12.410 --> 56:14.370
The previous scene is taking a bit longer.

56:14.453 --> 56:17.415
We don't know what we'll see
at the end of it, either.

56:18.249 --> 56:20.042
None of us know

56:21.002 --> 56:22.670
until we try.

56:24.755 --> 56:27.174
JEONG-A WAS INCREDIBLE ON THE SET.
I COULD FEEL HER FOCUS AND PASSION

56:32.054 --> 56:34.098
We make endless calculations

56:35.224 --> 56:37.643
to brace ourselves
for the craziness of life

56:38.686 --> 56:40.855
wonder all the "what ifs"

56:41.856 --> 56:45.818
and just hope for the best sometimes.

56:52.491 --> 56:53.659
Boo!

56:53.743 --> 56:57.413
But in the end, life seems to be a journey

56:58.205 --> 57:02.460
of learning to go forward
amidst all the uncertainty.

57:04.712 --> 57:08.549
Marriage seems to be the same.

57:10.968 --> 57:15.306
Of course, your lives together
will not always be smooth.

57:15.514 --> 57:18.559
You'll have as many sad days as happy ones

57:18.643 --> 57:22.563
and sometimes, you'll face surprises.

57:23.940 --> 57:25.358
But despite that

57:26.442 --> 57:30.446
if you trust each other,
prepare yourselves to go through anything

57:32.198 --> 57:36.911
and want to walk into the uncertain future
with each other

57:37.161 --> 57:38.955
I'd like to wish the couple

57:39.372 --> 57:43.793
nothing but the best until the end
as they courageously take on life.

57:44.085 --> 57:46.462
Congratulations on getting married.

57:59.183 --> 58:02.353
Groom and bride, march!

58:03.229 --> 58:04.939
Please give them a big applause.

58:45.855 --> 58:47.940
What a day it was, huh?

58:48.024 --> 58:49.108
Yeah.

58:49.442 --> 58:51.569
Seeing the bride laugh and cry

58:51.944 --> 58:54.280
made me realize
how big of a deal getting married was.

58:55.656 --> 58:59.577
I feel like I just saw
my child get married.

59:03.831 --> 59:05.708
- You did well.
- Yeah.

59:06.125 --> 59:08.502
Oh, you want to take a walk
before heading back?

59:08.586 --> 59:09.587
Sure.

59:10.129 --> 59:11.130
Here.

59:16.385 --> 59:20.139
What did you write in the speech
that you prepared?

59:20.431 --> 59:23.392
Oh, Eun-mi specifically asked me

59:23.476 --> 59:25.227
not to make her cry.

59:25.311 --> 59:26.312
I see.

59:26.395 --> 59:28.606
So, I took a very statistical approach.

59:29.732 --> 59:31.192
- You want to hear it?
- Yeah.

59:31.776 --> 59:35.571
"Korea has 50 million people,
15 of which whom are single.

59:35.905 --> 59:38.616
Half of them are men,
so, that's 7.5 million

59:38.824 --> 59:42.078
and assuming only 90% are straight
that leaves 6.8 million.

59:42.661 --> 59:46.957
So, what are the chances of you
falling in love with just one of them?"

59:48.209 --> 59:50.169
- That's a very slim chance.
- Exactly.

59:50.586 --> 59:51.879
That was my speech.

59:52.713 --> 59:55.299
That it was a miracle
for them to meet and fall in love.

01:00:00.221 --> 01:00:01.680
Oh, I have a present.

01:00:02.223 --> 01:00:03.224
What is it?

01:00:17.029 --> 01:00:18.114
It's beautiful.

01:00:18.364 --> 01:00:21.408
I wanted to give you one
since the first time I met you.

01:00:21.951 --> 01:00:24.912
It was a bit hard
to get your ring size, though.

01:00:25.287 --> 01:00:27.832
How did you figure it out?

01:00:31.210 --> 01:00:32.211
Thanks.

01:00:33.337 --> 01:00:34.463
You want to go with me?

01:00:34.672 --> 01:00:36.465
Yeah, take me!

01:00:37.133 --> 01:00:38.926
Bring me to New York, too.

01:00:39.927 --> 01:00:43.430
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

01:00:47.852 --> 01:00:49.019
We drank so much.

01:00:49.103 --> 01:00:50.312
This looks great.

01:00:50.396 --> 01:00:52.231
- I love you, Ui-yeong!
- Me too!

01:00:52.314 --> 01:00:53.357
Love you!

01:00:54.108 --> 01:00:55.276
I love you, Chef!

01:00:55.359 --> 01:00:56.402
Me too.

01:00:57.236 --> 01:00:59.572
- You have to come back.
- I love you extra, Tae-seop!

01:01:06.996 --> 01:01:08.122
Hello, sir.

01:01:08.581 --> 01:01:09.582
Oh, hi!

01:01:10.457 --> 01:01:12.877
- Did you finally get her ring size?
- Yeah.

01:01:20.926 --> 01:01:22.261
That's her size.

01:01:22.344 --> 01:01:24.680
Oh, this is her size?

01:01:32.897 --> 01:01:34.481
Give me your hand. I'll put it on.

01:01:52.291 --> 01:01:53.334
Is this it?

01:01:56.420 --> 01:01:58.255
The moment my friends described?

01:02:14.104 --> 01:02:15.105
Here.

01:02:17.691 --> 01:02:18.692
What do you think?

01:02:22.947 --> 01:02:24.990
- Tae-seop.
- Yeah?

01:02:31.205 --> 01:02:34.416
I don't just like you.

01:02:34.625 --> 01:02:36.752
I love you deeply.

01:02:37.544 --> 01:02:41.173
How do you always know and prepare
exactly what I need?

01:02:41.382 --> 01:02:43.425
Because I'm always watching you.

01:02:43.717 --> 01:02:45.928
Me? Her boyfriend.

01:02:46.011 --> 01:02:47.638
And this is a drilling machine
for drilling holes.

01:02:47.721 --> 01:02:50.266
- I'm calling the cops! Three!
- Three.

01:02:50.391 --> 01:02:51.600
Hi, Sae-byeok.

01:02:51.684 --> 01:02:54.436
Let's build a relationship
the way we want.

01:02:54.895 --> 01:02:57.273
I couldn't stop thinking about you,
so here I am.

01:02:58.023 --> 01:03:00.025
I'm glad we met now.

01:03:05.197 --> 01:03:06.657
I like you.

01:03:06.991 --> 01:03:09.451
I like you, too.

01:03:09.535 --> 01:03:11.287
You can't sleep here!

01:03:21.839 --> 01:03:22.881
Tae-seop

01:03:23.841 --> 01:03:26.385
thanks for coming to look for me.

01:03:26.468 --> 01:03:27.469
Oh, gosh!

01:03:27.553 --> 01:03:28.554
I'm sorry!

01:03:33.309 --> 01:03:34.977
Hello, I'm Song Tae-seop.

01:03:36.061 --> 01:03:37.396
I'm Lee Ui-yeong.

01:03:41.066 --> 01:03:42.318
Ui-yeong

01:03:42.484 --> 01:03:45.404
how do you feel about dating me

01:03:45.904 --> 01:03:47.031
with marriage in mind?

01:03:49.658 --> 01:03:51.660
- Tae-seop.
- Yeah?

01:03:53.245 --> 01:03:54.330
Will you...

01:03:55.998 --> 01:03:57.958
be my boyfriend...

01:03:59.335 --> 01:04:00.502
with marriage in mind?

01:04:13.057 --> 01:04:14.099
Of course.

